              "exam_name": "NCERT Based",
              "question": "<p>Given&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {a}+ \\overrightarrow {b}+\\overrightarrow {c}+\\overrightarrow {d}=0\\)</span>, which one of the following is incorrect?</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {a}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {b}\\)</span>,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {c}\\)</span>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {d}\\)</span>&nbsp;must be null vectors.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>The magnitude of&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {a}+\\overrightarrow {c}\\)</span>&nbsp;equals the magnitude of&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {b}+\\overrightarrow {d}\\)</span>.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>The magnitude of&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {a}\\)</span>&nbsp;can never be greater than the sum of the magnitudes of&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {b}, \\overrightarrow {c}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {d}\\)</span>.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {b}+\\overrightarrow {c}\\)</span> must be coplanar with <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {a}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {d}\\)</span> if <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {a}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {d}\\)</span> are non-collinear, and must be collinear with <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {a}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\overrightarrow {d}\\)</span>if they are collinear.</td></tr></tbody></table>\r\n&nbsp;",
